    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d730-a3">

                <pb facs="1320" n="1196" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1196"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 287.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Saavedra.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-10-14"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 14,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: Referring to your excellency’s two
                    polite notes to myself, both of date of the 9th instant, I have the honor to
                    respectfully request your excellency to furnish me with a statement showing for
                    each of the seven fiscal years from 1873 to 1880 the amount of the product of
                    the 13 per cent, of the forty unities set apart for foreign reclamations, as
                    also the amount of said product distributed, and the amount of said product not
                    distributed, for each of said seven fiscal years.</p>
                <p>Desiring this statement for the official information of myself and of my
                    government, I with pleasure renew to your excellency the assurances of my high
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>JEHU BAKER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
